BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tow
DTSTART:20260326T020000Z
DTEND:20260326T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20260326T020000Z
UID:Gs9AKX5WTv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 115 mins (1h55m)\n\nRose Byrne delivers an unstoppab
 le performance as real-life unhoused hero\, Seattle-ite Amanda Ogle\, whos
 e fight to regain custody of her live-in automobile becomes an unforgettab
 le rallying cry for the little guy.  Q&A with the film team on Friday\, M
 arch 20\, following the 7pm screening. Guests include Producer Brent Stief
 el\, and real-life subjects Amanda and Avery Ogle\, and lawyer Kevin Egger
 s.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/tow\n\nEstimated start: 19:1
 5
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Oscar Shorts: Animated
DTSTART:20260325T233000Z
DTEND:20260326T012000Z
DTSTAMP:20260325T233000Z
UID:tLZC35FxdM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nFor the 21st consecutive year\, S
 hortsTV presents the Oscar-Nominated Short Films\, opening on February 20.
  With all three categories offered – Animated\, Live Action\, and Docume
 ntary – this is your annual chance to predict the winners (and have the 
 edge in your Oscar pool)! A perennial hit with audiences around the countr
 y and the world\, don’t miss this year’s selection of shorts. The Acad
 emy Awards take place Sunday\, March 15.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in
 -theaters/2026-oscar-nominated-shorts/2026-oscar-nominated-shorts-animatio
 n\n\nEstimated start: 16:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
